        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jansen%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village takes its name from Peter Jansen, a local rancher who helped lay out the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mynehistory.com/items/show/290"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1874-1875 Mennonites led by Cornelius and Peter Jansen settled the area, bringing a unique “line village” layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mynehistory.com/items/show/290"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Around 1900, a village called “Russian Lane” stretched 4½ miles and housed 42 houses, churches, and schools.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
